      "description": "Watch FC Midtjylland vs Besiktas highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 30, 2026. The UEFA Europa League group stage brought FC Midtjylland and Besiktas together on July 30, 2026 , for a high-stakes encounter. Both teams displayed a cautious yet energetic start, aware that early momentum could define their continental campaigns in a clash of styles and tactical discipline. A Tight Opening and Disciplinary Struggles The first half was a gritty affair where clear-cut chances were scarce, and the referee was kept busy by a series of fouls. FC Midtjylland found themselves under pressure early on, leading to a yellow card for Mads Bech in the 35th minute following a handball. The situation grew more precarious for the hosts just before the interval when Martin Erlic was booked for a dangerous challenge. Despite the tension, the teams headed into the break with the deadlock unbroken, though the disciplinary tightrope was becoming a major concern for the Danish side. Red Card Reshapes the Contest The match reached a turning point in the 53rd minute when Martin Erlic received his second yellow card and was sent off. This forced FC Midtjylland into survival mode, and while manager Vincenzo Italiano introduced fresh legs like Kjell Waetjen and Han-Beom Lee to steady the ship, Besiktas sensed blood. The visitors' patience was rewarded in the 70th minute when substitute Milot Rashica clinical finish found the back of the net after a clever assist from Junior Olaitan . Building on their lead, the Turkish giants doubled their advantage just six minutes later. A penalty was awarded following a foul by Rasmus Nissen , and Orkun Kokcu stepped up to power the ball past Elias Olafsson from the spot. Late frustrations saw Vincenzo Italiano booked for dissent, but Besiktas remained professional, controlling the tempo until the final whistle to secure a well-earned victory on the road."
